  "answer": "The station USGS-01646500, located on the POTOMAC RIVER NEAR WASH, DC LITTLE FALLS PUMP STA, has a mean discharge of 320.7738 m3/s over the period from 1930-03-01 to 2026-10-24. The record shows no significant trend in the annual mean or annual maxima. The Q95 value is 35.7 m3/s, exceeded 95% of the time. The flood frequency analysis shows return levels for 2, 5, 10, 25, 50, and 100 years with GEV (GEV fitted by L-moments) and LP3 (Log-Pearson III) methods. The 100-year return level using the GEV method is 11247.39 m3/s and for LP3 is 10795.57 m3/s."
